<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Beylik of Shahrisabz</h1><p class="st-meta">1856 CE – 1870 CE (approx.) · capital Shahrisabz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kenagas Uzbek beylik around Shahrisabz that defied the emirs of Bukhara until Russia conquered it in 1870.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrisabz">Shahrisabz</a>, the old city of Kesh and birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, was the stronghold of the Kenagas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> tribe, which long resisted the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-bukhara">Manghit Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>. In the mid-19th century the Kenagas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">beks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jura-beg">Jura Beg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baba-beg">Baba Beg</a> established effective independence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">beks</a> ruled a fertile oasis on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashkadarya">Qashqadarya</a> with the neighbouring town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a>, fortifying it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>. They exploited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s conflicts with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>, at times accepting nominal Bukharan overlordship. Little is recorded of their internal government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1870 a Russian force under General Abramov stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrisabz">Shahrisabz</a> and handed it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-bukhara">Emirate of Bukhara</a>, then a Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jura-beg">Jura Beg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baba-beg">Baba Beg</a> fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1856 CE – 1870 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.64%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1856 CE – 1870 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shahrisabz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jura Beg, Baba Beg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Uzbek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shahrisabz Beylik, Kenagas beylik</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1863&amp;focus=beylik-of-shahrisabz" aria-label="Beylik of Shahrisabz on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6335 777 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Beylik of Shahrisabz lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6655 1033L6588 1010M6655 1033L6487 457"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6588 1010h0M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6655 1033h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6655 1033h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Shahrisabz. <a href="/atlas?year=1863&amp;focus=beylik-of-shahrisabz">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
